<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 180,000 t of wheat, 56,000 t barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 180,000 t of wheat, 56,000 t barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 120,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat and 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>The agency also bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. barley and 36,000 tonnes of Australian barley.</p>
<p>These are for March shipment. The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 120,000	 Western white	  60,000</p>
<p>				  Dark northern spring 25,000</p>
<p>				  Ordinary		 15,000</p>
<p>				  Hard red winter	20,000</p>
<p> Canada	40,000	1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>							     40,000</p>
<p> Australia   20,000	  Standard white	20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> U.S.	  20,000	  Feed		    20,000</p>
<p> Australia   36,000	  Feed		    36,000</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk, +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
